dsh-connections includes adapted portions and control behavior of DeepSeek Harness:

  @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-settings 0.2.1-rc.2 / 0.2.1-rc.3 / 0.2.1-rc.5
    Remote settings bootstrap; the ConfigForms accessor projects local interface
    preferences before native consumers activate. The snapshot-store dependency
    is explicitly supplied by Connections, not imported from a Client package.

  @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives 0.2.1-rc.5
    Connections-owned controls adapt composition, focus/Tab, menu and modal
    behavior, layout patterns and relative-time buckets from the published
    keyboard-composition, useModalLayer, focus, Menu, Modal and relativeTime
    implementations. Classes are plugin-prefixed; styling uses theme aliases.
    The simple control SVG paths are original Connections artwork.

Copyright (c) 2026 DeepSeek. These adapted portions are licensed under the MIT
License. The original control license is included as dist/native-ui.LICENSE in
both archives. The remote archive also includes dist/native-settings.LICENSE.

The native sidebar and Account providers, components and styles remain supplied
and owned by Harness; their factories are not copied. The shortcut adapter checks
and narrows the installed content/Settings command resolvers without copying or
replacing the native keyboard provider.

Source: https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/tree/dsh-v0.2.1-rc.5
The retained Settings bootstrap is composed by scripts/native-settings.mjs.
dist/native-inputs.json records exact native input versions, SHA-512 digests and
explicit compatibility boundaries. These records do not grant compatibility with
future Harness versions; the remaining constructor/shortcut seams need review
when their upstream inputs change.
